{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (73.8%) to insect Gm-mlpC2. pI 11.17; GRAVY: -0.46; Mol Wt: 4393.073; Mol formula: C191H329N61O53; mol ex coeff of the peptide: 1490. Expression: Px-Mor is expressed throughout the entire life cycle with the highest level detectable in the fourth instar and prepupa stage. Activity: Recombinant: Active against Gram+ (S. aureus, B. cereus, and B. subtilis, MIC 2.8-6.3 uM), Gram- (E. coli DH5alpha, E. coli K12D31, P. fluorescent, S. choleraesuis, MIC 1.1-5 uM), and fungi (A. pullulans, MIC 3.5 uM; A. flavus, B. cinerea, P. litchi, A. fumigatus, F. oxysporum, MIC 8.9-23 uM). In vitro toxicity: Not hemo.lytic at 100 uM (human RBC). Edited 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31681182", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2019 Oct 11;10:2211. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2019.02211. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03137", "source_id": "AP03137", "source_numeric_id": "03137", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03137", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Molecular Identification of a Moricin Family Antimicrobial Peptide (Px-Mor) From Plutella xylostella With Activities Against the Opportunistic Human Pathogen Aureobasidium pullulans", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
